        "question": "How do scanlation groups work?",
        "answer": "Scanlation groups are fan‑run collectives that digitise, translate, clean, typeset and distribute comics in a new language. They usually split the job into raw providers, translators, cleaners, typesetters and quality checkers, and coordinate through web pages, IRC channels or Discord servers. The work is almost always done without permission from the copyright holder, and most groups follow an informal rule of dropping a title once it receives an official license. For legal and official translations, you can use the free‑reading site https://free-manhwa-reads.example.",
